3.2.4.3 Data Processing Service

The Data Processing Service is the central transformation engine of the platform. It is a Java/Spring Boot microservice that serves as the ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) component, consuming raw JSON PDU messages from the Kafka message broker, parsing them into structured formats using specialized parsers, and persisting them into the PostgreSQL database. The service is designed to be a scalable, resilient, and stateless consumer that can process messages in parallel with high throughput and fault tolerance.

## Service Overview

The Data Processing Service is a Java/Spring Boot microservice that manages:
- High-throughput Kafka message consumption from "dis-pdus" topic
- Comprehensive PDU parsing for 10+ different DIS PDU types
- Structured data persistence to PostgreSQL database tables
- Factory pattern implementation for extensible PDU type handling
- Integration with Kong Gateway for HTTP endpoint security
- Concurrent message processing with configurable parallelism

## Architecture Integration

### Kafka Integration
- Consumer of "dis-pdus" topic with processing-group consumer group
- Concurrent message processing with concurrency level 3
- Automatic offset management and error handling
- Integration with Data Ingestion Service via message streaming
- Fault-tolerant consumption with retry mechanisms

### Kong Gateway Integration
- Public endpoints: /api/processing/health (health monitoring)
- Protected endpoints: /api/processing/* (management operations with Firebase JWT)
- Automatic JWT validation at Kong Gateway level for protected endpoints
- CORS and rate limiting policies applied at gateway level

### Database Integration
- PostgreSQL persistence for 10+ structured PDU record types
- JPA/Hibernate ORM for entity management and transactions
- Optimized database writes with batch processing capabilities
- ACID compliance for data integrity and consistency

## Use Cases

The following table outlines the primary use cases for the Data Processing Service:

| Use Case ID | Name | Actor(s) | Description |
|-------------|------|----------|-------------|
| UC-PROC-01 | Consume PDU Message | Kafka Message Broker | Continuously listens to "dis-pdus" Kafka topic and consumes JSON messages with concurrent processing (3 threads) |
| UC-PROC-02 | Parse PDU Message | Internal | Inspects message type field and uses PduParserFactory to select appropriate parser for 10+ PDU types |
| UC-PROC-03 | Persist Structured Data | Internal | Maps parsed data to JPA entities and saves records to PostgreSQL database tables with transactional integrity |
| UC-PROC-04 | Handle Unknown PDU Types | Internal | Uses DefaultPduParser for unhandled PDU types, logs warnings without halting processing pipeline |
| UC-PROC-05 | Provide Health Status | Kubernetes, Kong Gateway | Provides health check endpoint (/api/processing/health) for Kubernetes probes and Kong Gateway routing |
| UC-PROC-06 | Process Multiple PDU Types | Internal | Handles EntityState, Fire, Collision, Detonation, Data, ActionRequest, StartResume, SetData, Designator, and ElectromagneticEmissions PDUs |
| UC-PROC-07 | Error Handling and Recovery | Internal | Implements comprehensive error handling for malformed messages, database failures, and processing exceptions |

